<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21185] Immutable/append-only files can be modified through ATTR_FORCE</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21185</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When an admin marks a file "immutable" (chattr +i) or "append-only"&lt;br/&gt;
(chattr +a), normal users should not be able to change it unless they&lt;br/&gt;
have the special CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE permission.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But there's a loophole: the client sometimes sends a flag called&lt;br/&gt;
ATTR_FORCE with its request (for example, when clearing setuid/setgid&lt;br/&gt;
bits after a write, or during HSM import). Because the client controls&lt;br/&gt;
this flag, a normal user can set it and the MDS will let the change&lt;br/&gt;
through anyway, even though the file is marked immutable or&lt;br/&gt;
append-only and the user does not have the right permission.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
